quad y(0)=3\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495382 1072 #uuid "0f2dc972-31dc-57c9-9e22-2efe43c996b3" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495382 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 2 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =2 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =2 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =2\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =2 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 2 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(2 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{2+C}{1} \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2 + e^{- x}.\n$$" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495383 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495381 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495383 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495466 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495383 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495383 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)y=\\frac{4 x}{5},\\quad y(0)=-6\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495383 1072 #uuid "0f568c95-a616-5b36-b27c-7ed5df478cdc" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495383 1074 "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{5}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{4 x}{5}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\frac{x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{5}y) & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\cdot \\frac{4 x}{5} \\\\ e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5}y & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}) & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{x^{2}}{10}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}} & =\\int 4e^u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}} & =4e^u+C \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}} & =4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{10}})+C}{(e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{10}})} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - 10 e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{10}}.\n$$" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495384 1080 "e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495384 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495384 1083 #uuid "10762d6d-5f37-53c0-b521-e9659ffcb04a" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495385 1080 "\\left(4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} + 1\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495385 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495385 1083 #uuid "136f8070-e038-59b5-9fae-cc4aac2ce567" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495386 1080 "e^{x}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495386 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495386 1083 #uuid "144d0822-f694-5e68-9bbf-5a7bcbcfeb5c" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495387 1080 "4 - 10 e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{10}}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495387 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495387 1083 #uuid "1541a2f8-6088-5d7a-a8b1-2ba1bf8e634c" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495388 1080 "\\frac{x^{2}}{6}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495388 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495388 1083 #uuid "1606c6b9-4509-53c6-9b3c-5ce2d6e88a52" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495389 1080 "6 - 9 e^{- x}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495389 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495389 1083 #uuid "1c39dc7b-1910-5aa2-b559-13bc4f97e9f1" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495390 1080 "e^{6 x}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495390 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495390 1083 #uuid "1c5042ce-f847-5c29-9acf-80f90e962e0c" 13194139