{2}}{6}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3}y & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}) & =\\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{x^{2}}{6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4 x e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} & =\\int 4e^u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} & =4e^u+C \\\\ ye^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}} & =4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\right) e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6}})+C}{(e^{\\frac{(0)^{2}}{6}})} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{6}}.\n$$" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495421 1080 "e^{2 x}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495421 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495421 1083 #uuid "57e80fab-97cd-5361-bb79-7f984ac78102" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495422 1080 "e^{- x}" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495422 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495422 1083 #uuid "59dec3ff-8460-51e7-a903-42017b8930fe" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495423 1080 "x" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495423 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495423 1083 #uuid "5c5a2b3e-27d8-5b42-8795-8b6fed5d4789" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495424 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495482 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495424 1068 #