& =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 6 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =6 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =6 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =6\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =6 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 6 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(6 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6 - 10 e^{- x}.\n$$" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495379 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495401 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495403 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495433 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495461 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1077 "field-2" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495433 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495480 1079 #uuid "dc1dedd2-d5a5-512a-9220-be1c8471e402" 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495481 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495402 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495481 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495480 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [17592186495481 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535323 17592186045443 true] [175921864954